  "issue_title": "[bug] Duplicate-detection gate (Gate 3) is defeated by re-rolling SVF scales",
  "issue_body": "**Describe the bug**\n\nGate 3 (`_check_duplicate` in `scripts/pr_eval.py`) enforces the \"original work\" rule by cosine-comparing a submission against every prior head, rejecting matches above `_COPY_THRESHOLD = 0.999`. But it compares the **concatenated** `[head_weights (6\u00d71024=6144), svf_scales (7168)]` vector as a single cosine.\n\nThe SVF singular-value scales start at the identity (all `1.0`) and move only a little during CMA-ES, so **every** submission's SVF block is near-identical to every other's \u2014 and it is the *larger* of the two blocks, so it dominates the cosine. The routing **head** \u2014 the actual trained artifact that decides which pool model/role each query is sent to, i.e. the thing \"original work\" is about \u2014 is a minority of the norm and gets swamped.\n\n**Consequence (copy evasion):** an attacker can copy a rival's winning head **verbatim** and re-roll only the meaningless SVF scales. Head cosine is `1.0` (a literal copy), but the concatenated cosine falls to **~0.9986 < 0.999**, so the copied head **passes Gate 3**. The same swamping can also push two honest, genuinely-different heads over the threshold when SVF is tight (false positives).\n\n**Expected vs actual**\n- Expected: copying another miner's trained head is rejected as a duplicate.\n- Actual: a verbatim head copy with re-rolled SVF scales is accepted.\n\n**To reproduce**\n\nPure numpy, no GPU/API:\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\ndef cos(a, b):\n    a, b = a.ravel(), b.ravel()\n    return float(a @ b / (np.linalg.norm(a) * np.linalg.norm(b)))\n\nr = np.random.default_rng(1)\nhead_king = r.normal(0, 0.05, 6144)          # a rival's trained head\nsvf_king  = 1.0 + r.normal(0, 0.02, 7168)    # near-identity SVF\nsvf_copy  = 1.0 + np.random.default_rng(9).normal(0, 0.05, 7168)  # re-rolled SVF\n\nking = np.concatenate([head_king, svf_king])\ncopy = np.concatenate([head_king, svf_copy]) # SAME head, different SVF\n\nprint(\"head cosine  :\", cos(head_king, head_king))  # 1.0  (verbatim copy)\nprint(\"concat cosine:\", cos(king, copy))            # ~0.9986  -> under 0.999 gate\nprint(\"caught?      :\", cos(king, copy) > 0.999)    # False  <-- copy slips through\n```\n\n**Suggested fix**\n\nCompare the **head blocks** directly (gate on head cosine), since the head is the trained routing artifact. Keep the SVF cosine only as reported context, never as something that can mask a copied head. Add a head-shape guard so non-comparable prior heads are skipped.\n\n**Environment**\n- Python: 3.12\n- CPU only (gate runs before any GPU/API work)\n- Commit: `4c06e9e` (current `main`)",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-10T13:25:28.000Z",
